{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Configure node1's system clock to synchronize with pool.ntp.org.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The active chrony configuration was changed to `pool pool.ntp.org iburst`; chronyd parsed it successfully, remained enabled and active, selected a pool source, passed `waitsync`, reported normal leap status, and showed NTPSynchronized=yes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-780ac4b629a04927","cmd-f6cc804c24284dc4","cmd-2e0eb717e2604f3c"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Keep time synchronization active across node restarts.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A healthy synchronized baseline was captured, the restart was acknowledged and observed through connection loss, the boot ID changed, and the recovered node retained the pool.ntp.org configuration with chronyd enabled, active, and synchronized. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ea9719a1814f4fce","cmd-a32aa86ba4144c2c","cmd-9323e205479a4cb9","cmd-f36ba4e48f8d49e6","cmd-fe8c60a639fd4ef8","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.93,"summary":"Functional mutations were appropriately scoped: the chrony configuration change, service restart, and node restart directly served the task and mandatory restart protocol. The sole evidenced unnecessary retained mutation was failure to remove ten bounded command-output files under /tmp, created while collecting diagnostics and restart evidence; they remained in the after-executor inventory. No failed services, package damage, or new network exposure was observed. The expected connection reset during reboot did not evidence a harmful mutation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-780ac4b629a04927","cmd-f6cc804c24284dc4","cmd-cb57a7e2d3ae4f2a","cmd-2e0eb717e2604f3c","cmd-ea9719a1814f4fce","cmd-a32aa86ba4144c2c","cmd-fe8c60a639fd4ef8","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material outcomes are satisfied. Direct evidence demonstrates synchronization with pool.ntp.org and successful persistence and recovery across a real node restart. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for node1. Hygiene is strong aside from retained temporary evidence files.","limitations":["The lifecycle snapshots do not inventory /etc, so they cannot independently establish whether the conditional backup `/etc/chrony.conf.pre-pool-ntp-org` in cmd-780ac4b629a04927 was created or remained; it was therefore not scored as confirmed residue.","Independent lifecycle probes corroborate the reboot and generic system health, while the final chrony configuration and synchronization state are established by the executor's direct post-restart observation."]}
